<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-grip-method" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Grip Method</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      The Grip Method gives you four moveable chord shapes — Grips 1a, 2a, 1b, and 2b — that cover
      every rootless major-7th and Lydian-dominant (maj7b5)  voicing across the whole keyboard.
      <em>Category A grips</em> (1a and 2a) stack the chord tones 3–5–7–9 ascending from the
      bottom button. <em>Category B grips</em> (1b and 2b) re-voice the same four tones as 7–9–3–5,
      keeping the lower two notes in place while the upper two move up by an octave.
      Moving any grip up or down the isometric layout transposes it without changing its fingering shape.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-grip-method-four-grips">
    <title>The Four Core Grips</title>

    <p>
      The grids below show four important grips that will be used in progressions later in this section with different base notes. The chord produced by the grip is dependant on the bass note (not shown in grid below).
      Highlighted buttons are the chord tones; the label above each grid shows the grip name
      and quality; the label below shows the note names and their chord-tone functions.
    </p>

    <figure xml:id="fig-gm-all-four">
      <caption>(The Lydian Dominant grip is a maj7 voicing with a flattened 5th)</caption>
      <sidebyside widths="22% 22% 22% 22%" margins="5%">

        <!-- ========== Grip 1a: Cat A maj7 — F A C E (3 5 7 9) ========== -->
        <stack>
          <image xml:id="img-gm-grip1a">
            <latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.66, transform shape]
\pgfmathsetmacro{\isoangle}{60}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vv}{8}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hh}{6}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vlen}{0.85}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ang}{\isoangle/2}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\dlen}{(\vlen/2) / sin(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hlen}{(\vlen/2) / tan(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\xmax}{\hh*\hlen}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ymax}{\vv*\vlen}
%% — fixed-extent edge marks (identical x in all four grids → uniform crop width) —
\fill[gray!18] (0,{4*\vlen}) circle (0.04);
\fill[gray!18] (\xmax,{4*\vlen}) circle (0.04);
%% — title above grid —
\node[font=\normalsize\bfseries, align=center]
  at ({\xmax/2},{9.8*\vlen}) {Grip 1a};
\node[font=\small, align=center]
  at ({\xmax/2},{9.15*\vlen}) {Category A \textbullet{} Major 7th};
%% — grid and all note buttons —
\drawgridandnotes
\gn{5}{1.5}{C}{0}
\gn{4}{2}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{3}{2.5}{D}{0}
\gn{2}{3}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{3.5}{E}{0}
\gn{5}{2.5}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{3}{E}{0}
\gn{3}{3.5}{\shortstack{\textbf{F}\\{\scriptsize\bfseries 3rd}}}{1}
\gn{2}{4}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{4.5}{G}{0}
\gn{5}{3.5}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{4}{G}{0}
\gn{3}{4.5}{A$\flat$, G$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{2}{5}{\shortstack{\textbf{A}\\{\scriptsize\bfseries 5th}}}{1}
\gn{1}{5.5}{B$\flat$, A$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{5}{4.5}{A}{0}
\gn{4}{5}{B$\flat$, A$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{3}{5.5}{B}{0}
\gn{2}{6}{\shortstack{\textbf{C}\\{\scriptsize\bfseries 7th}}}{1}
\gn{1}{6.5}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{5}{5.5}{C}{0}
\gn{4}{6}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{3}{6.5}{D}{0}
\gn{2}{7}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{7.5}{E}{0}
\gn{5}{6.5}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{7}{\shortstack{\textbf{E}\\{\scriptsize\bfseries 9th}}}{1}
\gn{3}{7.5}{F}{0}
\gn{2}{8}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{8.5}{G}{0}
%% — note-name summary below grid —
\node[font=\small\bfseries, align=center]
  at ({\xmax/2},{-0.55*\vlen}) {F \textbullet{} A \textbullet{} C \textbullet{} E};
\node[font=\scriptsize, align=center]
  at ({\xmax/2},{-1.15*\vlen}) {3rd \textbullet{} 5th \textbullet{} 7th \textbullet{} 9th};
\end{tikzpicture}
            </latex-image>
          </image>

          <image xml:id="img-gm-notation1a" source="notation/grip-1a" width="100%">
            <shortdescription>Staff notation for Grip 1a: F A C E</shortdescription>
          </image>
          <p><em>Grip 1a</em></p>
          <p>Cat A maj7 grip</p>
          <p> Dmaj9 if bass is D</p>
        </stack>

